; variant-set fixture. A discriminated form whose variant is selected by
; SEVERAL discriminant values: `(variant :when [a b] …)`.
;
; `:when` takes one symbol or a vector of symbols; selection is
; membership. This is WebGPU's own rule for `GPUPrimitiveState`:
; `stripIndexFormat` is read when the topology is a strip (and there
; are two strips), and ignored for the three list topologies. Before
; `:when` took a vector the rule could not be declared: one variant named
; one value, and two identical single-value variants collided on the key
; (`variant_key_collision`, rightly: two declarations of one slot can
; drift). One declaration reaching several values is what keeps that
; check exactly as strict as it is: a key still lives in one variant.
;
; A value selects at most one variant. The loader rejects an empty
; `:when []`, a repeat within one list, and a value two variants both
; list (all `invalid_manifest`), and the aggregate pass checks every
; listed value against the discriminant's member set, once per value
; (`unknown_discriminant_value` naming the offender, keeping the rest).
;
; The exporters do not multiply the branch: JSON Schema guards the one
; `if/then` with `enum` where a single value uses `const`, and lists the
; values under `x-sjon-discriminant`; TypeScript narrows the discriminant
; brand to `Symbol_<"triangle-strip" | "line-strip">`; Markdown heads the
; variant `:topology [triangle-strip line-strip]`, each spelled as the
; manifest was, so a single-value variant's output is byte-for-byte what
; it was before. The M2 schema-export demo regenerates
; `variant-set.schema.json.golden`, `variant-set.d.ts.golden`,
; `variant-set.md.golden`, and `variant-set.export.json.golden` against
; this manifest.

(plugin :name variant-set :version "1.0.0"
  (value-kind :name topology
    :description "How vertices assemble into primitives: the five WebGPU topologies."
    :underlying symbol
    :members (member-set :values [point-list line-list line-strip triangle-list triangle-strip]))

  (value-kind :name index-format
    :description "The index buffer element type."
    :underlying symbol
    :members (member-set :values [uint16 uint32]))

  (form :name primitive
    :description "Primitive assembly state. `:topology` selects the variant; the strip-index-format key exists only under a strip."
    :discriminant topology
    (key :name topology :type topology :optional true :default triangle-list
      :description "Defaults to triangle-list, as GPUPrimitiveState does.")
    (key :name cull :type symbol :optional true :description "none / front / back.")
    (variant :when [triangle-strip line-strip]
      (key :name strip-index-format :type index-format :optional true
        :description "The primitive-restart index format; only meaningful when the topology is a strip."))))
